---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/apps/marsello';
const title = "Marsello for Shopify: loyalty balances, store identity and SMS";
const desc = "Evaluate loyalty-led marketing across ecommerce and POS, with a practical acceptance plan for rewards and customer identity.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does loyalty membership permit SMS marketing?",
    "answer": "No. Keep loyalty membership and channel permission separate and check eligibility before dispatch."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should a Marsello demonstration prove?",
    "answer": "Ask for a traceable earning, redemption and refund ledger, correct tier treatment and redemption only at authorized locations."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is Marsello only an SMS sender?",
    "answer": "Its current offering combines loyalty with marketing capabilities. Confirm the purchased email, SMS, POS and location scope for your account."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/apps">App directory</a>
    <p class="badge mt-6">Operating review · November 25, 2026</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p>
  </section>
  <article class="container prose-shopify pb-16">
    <h2>Why loyalty changes the SMS decision</h2>
    <p>The <a class="link" href="https://apps.shopify.com/marsello">Marsello Shopify listing</a> describes points, rewards and VIP tiers alongside email and SMS marketing. Its value is connecting benefits to customer activity across online and physical sales, rather than simply adding another broadcast tool. A retailer with an existing rewards program should first decide whether Marsello will own that program or only consume its data.</p>
    <h2>Separate membership from permission</h2>
    <p>A member can hold a reward without being subscribed to promotional texts. Keep customer identity, account access, points balance and channel permissions distinct. Ask which identifier links Shopify checkout, POS and the customer portal, how duplicate profiles are resolved and which system wins a conflict. A shared household phone number should not silently transfer another member’s benefits.</p>
    <h2>Define the benefit before writing the message</h2>
    <p>Marsello’s <a class="link" href="https://www.marsello.com/customer-loyalty">loyalty product page</a> describes configurable earning rules, reward conditions and a customer portal. Write the qualifying purchase, exclusions, redemption location and expiry rule in plain language before announcing a benefit. Match the portal balance and staff instructions to the message; a relevant reminder is useful only if the customer can redeem what it promises.</p>
    <h2>Proposed acceptance exercise: loyalty ledger</h2>
    <p>Create controlled online and POS purchases for one member. Record order identifiers, eligible spend, points earned and redemption entries. Replay an order update and inspect whether points duplicate. Compare the ledger with receipts and the customer-facing balance. These are proposed procurement checks, not tests we performed or guarantees about connector behavior.</p>
    <h2>Proposed acceptance exercise: refund and tier boundary</h2>
    <p>Place a qualifying order near a tier threshold, redeem a reward, then partially refund the order. Ask the vendor to demonstrate the expected balance and tier treatment, including a refund after points have already been spent. Agree how negative balances, expired benefits and manual staff corrections are handled. Preserve an audit trail that explains a customer dispute without requiring staff to infer the original calculation.</p>
    <h2>Proposed acceptance exercise: cross-store authorization</h2>
    <p>Have a member earn online and attempt redemption at a second location. Verify the actual supported integration, allowed locations and staff access. Try an excluded product and an unauthorized staff role. A multisite account does not itself establish that every location, franchise or legal entity may redeem every reward; document the intended boundary before expanding the program.</p>
    <h2>Use loyalty context without creating another offer</h2>
    <p>A points reminder can explain an existing benefit instead of issuing a new blanket discount. Decide whether email or SMS is appropriate for that member and check current permission and dispatch eligibility separately from membership. Suppress a queued reward reminder after redemption or expiry. Coordinate with the existing sender so one reward event does not produce competing messages; see <a class="link" href="/guides/email-sms-coordination">channel coordination</a>.</p>
    <h2>Price the operating footprint</h2>
    <p>Use the current <a class="link" href="https://www.marsello.com/pricing">Marsello pricing page</a> and a written quote for your locations, customer count, marketing scope and SMS destinations. Ask what additional sites, connectors, messages and onboarding cost. A loyalty subscription is a fixed commitment even in a quiet sending month. Include staff reconciliation time and the cost of honoring earned benefits during any transition.</p>
    <h2>Evaluate incremental contribution and reward liability</h2>
    <p>For a proposed pilot, assign eligible members to treatment and holdout before reminders are sent. Compare contribution per assigned member over the same repeat-purchase window, using net sales after discounts and refunds less product and variable fulfillment costs. Deduct incremental messaging, reward fulfillment and support costs once. Then subtract the fixed subscription and setup allocation at program level. Track outstanding points separately; do not treat every unredeemed point as either immediate profit or a cash expense equal to face value.</p>
    <h2>Choose on demonstrable reward continuity</h2>
    <p>Shortlist Marsello when loyalty and physical-store activity are central to the customer experience. Require a reconciled opening ledger, an agreed refund policy, a supported location map and an accountable owner for disputed benefits. Export balances and permissions before changing systems and reconcile them afterward; account connection alone does not prove migration completeness. Review <a class="link" href="/guides/pricing">pricing economics</a> alongside the quote rather than choosing from a universal app rank.</p>
    <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
